{-# OPTIONS --safe #-}
module DASHI.Physics.YangMills.BalabanCMP98Equation119MultiscaleInstallationRound147Exact where

------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- ROUND147 A1: THE LATTICE Eq. (119) OPERATOR IS ROUND126'S ONE-STEP Q'
--
-- Round126 proves the noncommutative finite product rule
--
--   Q_k' = sum_j Q_{k-1} ... Q_{j+1} Q'_j Q_{j-1} ... Q_0
--
-- for an abstract additive operator carrier.  Round146 realizes CMP98
-- Eq. (119) on the repository's actual periodic lattice.  This module joins
-- them: it builds the Round126 carrier out of the lattice Lie-algebra bond
-- fields, installs
--
--   q_j      := the CMP98 (125) block-path average at scale j,
--   qPrime_j := the Round146 realization of Eq. (119) at scale j,
--
-- and records that the installed one-step derivative *is* the Eq. (119)
-- expression on every positively oriented coarse bond, definitionally.
--
-- Consequently the multiscale derivative Q_k' supplied by Round126 is, on this
-- carrier, the literal insertion sum of the source's one-step derivatives; no
-- further scalar Q' receipt is involved.
--
-- What is still a modelling convention, and is stated as such: the source
-- defines its coarse objects on positively oriented bonds, while the
-- repository's bond fields are total on directed bonds, so `fromCoarseValues`
-- extends a coarse value function to reversed bonds by the sign convention
-- A(reverse b) = - A(b).  Every path used by Eq. (119) and by the block-path
-- average is built from positive bonds only, so no value used by either
-- operator depends on that extension.
------------------------------------------------------------------------

open import Agda.Builtin.Equality using (_≡_; refl)
open import Agda.Builtin.Nat using (Nat)
open import Data.Nat.Base using (NonZero)

open import DASHI.Physics.YangMills.CompactLieProofLevel
